WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.047
GARCH, one comma one, says today's variance h t is built from three pieces.

00:00:05.497 --> 00:00:06.760
A constant omega.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.490
Alpha times yesterday's squared shock.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.089
And beta times yesterday's variance.

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:15.239
Let's hit the model with a single shock and watch.

00:00:15.689 --> 00:00:19.588
Variance jumps, then decays back towards its long-run level.

00:00:20.038 --> 00:00:22.852
Alpha controls how hard the model reacts to news.

00:00:23.302 --> 00:00:25.243
Turn it up and the spike gets taller.

00:00:25.693 --> 00:00:27.069
Beta controls memory.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:29.526
Turn it up and the decay gets slower.

00:00:29.976 --> 00:00:33.475
The sum, alpha plus beta, is the persistence.

00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:37.188
It must stay below one for the variance to settle down.

00:00:37.638 --> 00:00:44.787
For South Africa's training window, our fitted alpha is about 0.11 and beta about 0.87.

00:00:45.237 --> 00:00:47.929
Persistence is about 0.99.

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:51.171
A shock fades, but slowly, over weeks.

00:00:51.621 --> 00:00:55.323
That slow fade is exactly the clustering we saw in the opening.
